{
  "id": "32f2b5cc-b402-4ced-8541-ad37feeb5247",
  "ok": true,
  "result": {
    "issue": {
      "id": "8d392f70-de90-4b4c-981c-81ce19c980c5",
      "identifier": "SKI-16",
      "title": "Adopt ticket-protected direct regional DataFn transport in Skillplane",
      "url": "https://linear.app/21n/issue/SKI-16/adopt-ticket-protected-direct-regional-datafn-transport-in-skillplane",
      "description": "## Goal\n\nAfter [AUTH-2](https://linear.app/21n/issue/AUTH-2/expose-placement-bound-auth-context-for-regional-application-data) and [DATA-4](https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-4/support-gateway-issued-direct-regional-sync-tickets) are released, move steady-state first-party DataFn reads off the canonical gateway and onto the owning regional DataFn endpoint without weakening authentication, placement fencing, mutation safety, or observability.\n\n## Why\n\n[SKI-13](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SKI-13/refactor-skillplane-into-a-global-control-plane-and-regional-workspace) gives Skillplane canonical placement-aware routing and [SKI-2](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SKI-2/adopt-datafn-in-skillplanes-first-party-application-data-path) gives the app one typed DataFn read boundary, but every query still traverses the gateway. That preserves correctness while retaining an avoidable cross-region hop. [AUTH-2](https://linear.app/21n/issue/AUTH-2/expose-placement-bound-auth-context-for-regional-application-data) must first expose placement-bound authenticated context, and [DATA-4](https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-4/support-gateway-issued-direct-regional-sync-tickets) must first issue short-lived regional transport tickets. This issue is the Skillplane consumer work after those reusable platform contracts exist.\n\n## Implementation sequence\n\n 1. Consume the AuthFn placement-bound authenticated context rather than deriving a second product-local credential model.\n 2. Add one authenticated canonical DataFn bootstrap call at the existing shared app client boundary.\n 3. Resolve the server-owned registry entry and return only an expiry-bound `{ httpUrl, wsUrl, ticket, regionEpoch, expiresAt }` transport grant.\n 4. Expose dedicated public DataFn-only regional endpoints; keep application, AuthFn, MCP, and administrative cell endpoints private.\n 5. Enforce ticket signature, audience, subject, workspace, region, placement epoch, scopes, TTL, CORS, rate limiting, and DDoS controls at every regional endpoint.\n 6. Extend the Skillplane DataFn client transport with in-memory grant caching, proactive renewal, and canonical re-bootstrap on expiry, region/epoch mismatch, workspace movement, or the standard moved-tenant close/error signal.\n 7. Send query, permitted mutation, pull, push, reconcile, and WebSocket sync traffic directly to the owning region. Keep authentication, bootstrap, placement, public projections, and domain commands on the canonical gateway.\n 8. Add per-phase latency and route-provenance telemetry without logging tickets, cookies, or database URLs.\n 9. Add two-region end-to-end tests proving steady-state DataFn traffic bypasses the gateway, placement changes re-bootstrap safely, and mutations are never ambiguously replayed.\n10. Roll out behind a per-environment/per-workspace flag with canary comparison and instant fallback to canonical gateway transport.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n* The first authenticated DataFn request bootstraps through the canonical gateway and later requests use the ticket-authorized owning-region endpoint until renewal.\n* Regional endpoints accept no session cookie as authority and reject every ticket mismatch or stale placement epoch.\n* A moved workspace re-bootstrap is automatic and never replays an ambiguous mutation.\n* Auth, public pages, R2/domain commands, MCP, and administrative traffic remain canonical.\n* Two-region browser/integration evidence proves steady-state gateway bypass and measures bootstrap, gateway, regional, DataFn phase, and total latency separately.\n* Rollback switches the shared client boundary back to canonical `/datafn` without feature-level changes.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nBlocked by [AUTH-2](https://linear.app/21n/issue/AUTH-2/expose-placement-bound-auth-context-for-regional-application-data) and [DATA-4](https://linear.app/21n/issue/DATA-4/support-gateway-issued-direct-regional-sync-tickets). Related to [SKI-2](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SKI-2/adopt-datafn-in-skillplanes-first-party-application-data-path) and [SKI-13](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SKI-13/refactor-skillplane-into-a-global-control-plane-and-regional-workspace).",
