    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "089d2427-9eca-4251-80f5-f1b2de59f134",
        "body": "PR [#44](https://github.com/21nCo/skillplane/pull/44) implements the ticket-protected, read-only direct regional DataFn path with gateway-held Ed25519 signing, regional public-key verification, placement and membership fencing, canary controls, fallback, and telemetry. The exact branch was built and deployed to dev; signed-in India and US browser checks each completed one canonical bootstrap and one cookie-free direct regional query, while invalid, cross-region, excluded-workspace, and ticketless requests were rejected. `pnpm build`, focused app tests/typecheck/lint/format, topology validation, and `pnpm smoke:dev` passed; SKI-18 tracks an independent existing MCP Worker upload failure.\n",
        "bodyTruncated": false,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-21T05:00:51.502Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-21T05:00:51.489Z",
        "parentId": null,
        "user": {
          "id": "3a6ed003-6380-47ef-9e7b-b2b01ebddc6a",
          "displayName": "aravink",
          "avatarUrl": "https://public.linear.app/b8d3a0b7-a4ef-48ad-8dcf-cbefe8447e51/07eb2763-1f9b-44ad-a1cf-4f8d38fcad0b/a381d637-4a0a-4d20-9b85-490e90415cdd"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "94109e9b-fb4c-4de3-aad6-f185aa1f9ed3",
        "body": "Update to the 2026-09-16 blocker: the AUTH-2 consumer API is now published in `authfn@0.3.0` and `@authfn/multi-region@0.1.2`; DATA-4 remains available. I updated the matching AuthFn package set locally, added optional AuthFn placement-context and DataFn route-provider hooks, and added a server-owned DataFn-only endpoint field to the topology. The work is local and incomplete. AuthFn and control-plane unit tests pass (21 and 42); the affected package type checks pass.\n\nThe remaining blocker is a security contract decision: DATA-4's regional verifier requests an application identity separately from the route ticket, while SKI-16 forbids session-cookie authority on regional endpoints. Please confirm whether the verified short-lived ticket is the sole regional bearer credential or whether a separate regional application credential must be issued. I have not created a commit, push, or PR.\n",
        "bodyTruncated": false,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-20T05:12:44.367Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-20T05:12:44.357Z",
        "parentId": null,
        "user": {
          "id": "3a6ed003-6380-47ef-9e7b-b2b01ebddc6a",
          "displayName": "aravink",
          "avatarUrl": "https://public.linear.app/b8d3a0b7-a4ef-48ad-8dcf-cbefe8447e51/07eb2763-1f9b-44ad-a1cf-4f8d38fcad0b/a381d637-4a0a-4d20-9b85-490e90415cdd"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "4cd1dd74-7467-4161-9647-05962af1711a",
        "body": "Blocked before implementation: SKI-16 requires consuming the released AUTH-2 placement-bound authentication context. AUTH-2 is marked Done and its implementation was merged to Superfunctions dev, but the public registry still exposes only `authfn@0.2.0` and `@authfn/multi-region@0.1.1` (both published 2026-08-29); those package exports contain no placement-context issuer contract. The DATA-4 side is available in `@datafn/client@0.1.1` and `@datafn/server@0.1.3`.\n\nProceeding now would require either deriving a Skillplane-local credential model or depending on an unreleased Git revision, both contrary to this issue’s sequence and release prerequisite. The worktree remains clean; no files were changed and no tests were run. Unblock by publishing the AUTH-2 consumer API and naming the supported package/version, or by making an explicit alternative dependency decision.",
        "bodyTruncated": false,
